comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T11:30:20.669Z","harness:claude-code","GH-737 maps here (no new item). CodeFactor flagged 'Using a spread operator here creates a new array unnecessarily' at src/sdk/cli-contracts/flag-contracts.ts:113, commit 0d75347f.\n\nThe flagged construct is SUBCOMMAND_GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS, an array literal whose entire body is one spread of a mapped array:\n\n  export const SUBCOMMAND_GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS: CliFlagContract[] = [\n    ...RESERVED_EXTENSION_HOST_FLAGS.map((definition) => ({ ... })),\n  ];\n\nThe map already produces a new array; wrapping it in a literal copies it again. Reduces to dropping the brackets and the spread.\n\nMapped here rather than filed separately for two reasons. The file is this item's subject — the same per-command repetition this item exists to remove — so the restructuring will pass through this exact declaration. And the class already has an owner in the closed pm-zt1c (GH-553/GH-584, CodeFactor unnecessary-spread findings), so a fourth point item would fragment territory the registry already consolidated.\n\nWorth carrying into the fix: the two adjacent declarations show the same shape. GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS spreads SUBCOMMAND_GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS to append a single --version entry, which is legitimate, and the comment on GOVERNANCE_AND_CONTENT_FILTER_FLAG_CONTRACTS notes it is deliberately spread into two tables at a fixed position to preserve published contract order. Any dedupe must preserve that ordering guarantee — the published flag order is contract surface."
  "2026-07-27T10:05:40.122Z","harness:codex","Evidence: implementation is complete; pnpm lint passed with zero jscpd clones, static/docstring/SDK compatibility gates passed, 375 files and 6,404 tests passed at 100/100/100/100 coverage, and an unrelated packed consumer resolved its local executable then passed install/doctor/create/list plus npx and bunx version smoke tests."
  "2026-07-27T11:12:38.871Z","harness:codex","PR #769 review evidence: corrected the resolution to attribute only flag-contract deduplication to this item; SDK governance export consolidation remains correctly owned by pm-44aa4x."
  "2026-07-27T11:40:24.342Z","harness:codex","Final evidence after PR #769 review corrections: focused release contracts passed 51/51; focused merge SDK safety passed 19/19; pnpm test:coverage passed 375 files and 6,404 tests with 100% statements (44,294/44,294), branches (31,472/31,472), functions (9,064/9,064), and lines (43,029/43,029); pnpm lint passed ESLint, zero jscpd clones across 778 files, the 133 suppression ceiling, 100% docstrings, package-boundary, token-budget, SDK-surface/import-cost, and CLI-transport gates; git diff --check passed."
